WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.937
-Our next guest is a very funny
comedienne you can see

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.072
in her off-Broadway hit
one-woman show, "Kate,"

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.807
which is playing through
October 8th

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.675
at the Connelly Theater
here in New York.

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:10.744
Her FX comedy special

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:14.046
"Kate Berlant:
Cinnamon in the Wind"

00:00:14.046 --> 00:00:15.281
premieres today on Hulu.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.316
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.118
-I do comedy
primarily to process

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:19.351
the overwhelming privilege of my

00:00:19.351 --> 00:00:23.723
childhood, adolescence,
and now adulthood, right?

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.358
If you can imagine growing up

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:28.294
almost collapsing under
the weight of resources, right?

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:29.929
Almost so many -- right? --

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.297
that your gait
is affected, right?

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.332
If you can imagine my parents,
you know, so loving,

00:00:33.332 --> 00:00:35.001
"You're so special, we love
you," right?

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.202
They're actually
not divorced, right?

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.470
All of that.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.540
And somehow, with all of that
weighing you down,

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.509
just finding the strength
to get to Zara,

00:00:43.509 --> 00:00:46.746
just somehow -- Whoa!

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:50.083
-Please welcome back to the show
Kate Berlant, everybody.

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.118
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:07.433
What a joy to
have you here in person.

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.769
-Finally.
I'm so relieved to be back.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.403
-Yes.
-It's been hell being gone.

00:01:11.403 --> 00:01:12.772
-Yeah, the time away.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.640
-The time away.
But I learned a lot.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.343
-Oh, good.
I can tell you're different.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.312
-I'm different. I've changed.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.547
-And I liked you the first time,
so this is a big --

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:22.948
-It's better now.
-It's better now.

00:01:22.948 --> 00:01:25.885
-Trust me, it's better now.
-So, this is very exciting.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:28.887
This is a stand-up special
that is coming out

00:01:28.887 --> 00:01:29.889
tomorrow -- or today.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.190
Is it today?

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.325
-I think last night at midnight,
technically, so it's out.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.459
It's out.

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:34.760
-It's out.
-Yeah.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.897
-And how did you come up
with the title

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.599
"Cinnamon in the Wind?"

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:42.501
-I don't know.
-Okay.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:43.969
-Well, you know,
"Cinnamon in the Wind" --

00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:46.072
The special
is largely improvised.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.140
It's really just
captured one night.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.975
Bo Burnham directed it,
the brilliant Bo Burnham.

00:01:49.975 --> 00:01:51.077
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:52.912
-Yes, absolutely.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.380
Back to me, though. Back to me.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:58.317
And, so, "Cinnamon in the Wind"
is sort of ephemeral, right?

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:01.220
it sort of harkens to that
which is the nature of life

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.689
and perhaps the show, you know?

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.190
-That's really --
That's really --

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.258
Now it makes a lot of sense.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.859
-Yeah, yeah. That reads, yeah?

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:08.895
-So, I have this question,
because now you're doing

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:13.633
this one-woman show,
also directed by Bo Burnham,

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:16.569
and it does seem as though
it's a departure from stand-up,

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:20.406
and I'm assuming it must be
a bit of a leap.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.807
It must be nice to have
somebody like Bo,

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:23.876
who's done the other
with you, as well.

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:25.945
How did you come to the --
I don't know --

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.481
the conclusion to do something
that was similar to stand-up

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.249
and that it's just you
onstage but very different?

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:32.351
-Yes, well, the special --
Here's a little peek

00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:33.485
behind the curtain.

00:02:33.485 --> 00:02:36.623
The special was shot for FX
three years ago.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:38.958
-Okay.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:42.128
You are aging so well.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:43.630
I was watching and I was like,
"Okay, yeah."

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.830
It's terrifying.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.100
But we -- Well,
I don't know what happened.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.969
I think the suits were a little
scared about the material.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.203
They thought if people saw it --

00:02:51.203 --> 00:02:52.872
They wanted to keep
the public from my comedy.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:54.040
-Yeah.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.875
-But I told them,
"No, people have to see it."

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:59.746
They were afraid there'd be
an uprising if people saw it.

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.680
-Wow. So this is sort of
a three-year conversation

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:02.982
that you finally won.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.950
-Yeah. And, luckily -- You know,
typically, comedians,

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.853
you do a special,
it's put out immediately

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:09.889
because comedians are responding
to the times, right?

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:12.525
But my act was mostly me
crossing my eyes,

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.526
so I think we're okay that
the three years have passed.

00:03:14.526 --> 00:03:15.928
-Because that has not
gone out of style.

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:17.963
-No, no.
I still -- I can't knock that.

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:22.368
But the new show really is a --
It's theatrical.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:23.970
It's a play,
I guess you could say.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.072
-It's a really -- This is
a very theatrical photo.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.773
I'm very impressed with that.

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:30.209
-That's me, drama.
-Yeah.

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:31.544
-It is, like all art,

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:34.213
just a vain attempt to be
taken seriously.

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:35.281
And so this is really --

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.915
I'm trying to be like,
"I'm an actress."

00:03:36.915 --> 00:03:38.251
You know, so that's --

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.852
I'm really
white-knuckle gripping that.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:43.989
But it's a proper theater
show -- lights and excitement,

00:03:43.989 --> 00:03:46.559
and there's a little dancing
in there, yeah.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:50.629
-Your longtime friend and
collaborator, John Early,

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:53.632
who we're big fans of
on the show, as well --

00:03:53.632 --> 00:03:56.602
You and John obviously
communicate all the time.

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:59.438
Has he been supportive of
your new off-Broadway show?

00:03:59.438 --> 00:04:00.472
-It's been hard for John.

00:04:00.472 --> 00:04:03.075
-Yeah, because you're off
on your own.

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:06.211
-Seeing me shine.
-Yeah. Thrive even.

00:04:06.211 --> 00:04:07.614
-You really find out
who your friends are

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.182
when you put on
an off-Broadway show

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.950
after your special's been
shelved for three years.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.651
-Yeah.
-You really find out.

00:04:12.651 --> 00:04:16.055
And he's been threatened.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:17.857
No, it's been great.

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.625
He's my best friend.
He comes a lot.

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:22.962
He is, though --
We'll, very funnily, send texts.

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:24.830
Like, the day the show opened,
he sent texts --

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:29.301
a text to Bo and I that just
said, "Do not Google the show."

00:04:29.301 --> 00:04:32.538
And, so, he'll call me,
and I'll get a voicemail.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.407
He's like,
"Woke up with a bad feeling.

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:36.408
Tonight's not going to work.
I can feel it.

00:04:36.408 --> 00:04:37.910
Don't go out there."

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.879
So, that's very fun and...

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:41.847
-You grew up in L.A.

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:45.317
Did you always know that you
wanted to be an actor?

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:46.518
-How do I put this? Yeah.

00:04:46.518 --> 00:04:47.753
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:04:47.753 --> 00:04:49.521
-Did everyone around you
also know?

00:04:49.521 --> 00:04:50.723
-Everyone was like,
"You have it."

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:53.492
No, I just loved
attention very young,

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:56.295
striving for it at all times,
still you might say.

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:57.830
Can't get enough of it.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:01.100
And, so, yeah, I mean,
I wanted to be an actress,

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.835
but then comedy -- You know,
when you look like this,

00:05:03.835 --> 00:05:06.572
you know, when you make faces
like that constantly,

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.007
you will be pushed into comedy.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:11.377
So -- But, again,
the play is sort of me, again,

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:13.513
trying to demand an
acting career.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.147
-Well, there you go.
-Yeah.

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:17.850
-I mean, you do have an
acting career that started

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.286
when you were very young on
a little show called

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:21.354
"Lizzie McGuire."

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:22.655
-Oh, yes.

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:24.189
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:24.189 --> 00:05:27.693
-And do you remember
getting the part?

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:28.994
-How could I forget?
-Yeah.

00:05:28.994 --> 00:05:31.797
-It's the only part I've ever
booked from an audition,

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:33.532
essentially, truly.

00:05:33.532 --> 00:05:34.967
Yeah, I auditioned.

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:37.870
I believe the audition, I was
supposed to have two lines,

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.071
and then it became one.

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:41.674
-So you got a one-line part in
"Lizzie McGuire."

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:43.909
Can we -- We have the clip.
Do you mind if we show it?

00:05:43.909 --> 00:05:45.978
-I demand that you show it now.
-Okay.

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.881
Let's take a look at Kate in
"Lizzie McGuire."

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:51.017
-Hey, Lizzie, very cool pants.

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:52.151
-Her.

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:54.453
-Okay, so...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:54.453 --> 00:05:56.522
Now, just --
We do want to make sure,

00:05:56.522 --> 00:06:00.292
because I think the eye might be
drawn to the sort of

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:02.562
principal performers,
who are walking towards us.

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:05.164
-I think the eye
is just uncannily drawn to me.

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:06.299
You can't even see the whole --

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:08.367
-Just in case anybody missed it,

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.669
we do want to spotlight you
a little bit more.

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:12.638
Let's watch it one more time.

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:14.607
-Hey, Lizzie, very cool pants.

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:16.609
-Her.
-Wow. Really nicely done.

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:19.111
-There I am. Yeah.

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:21.080
[ Applause ]

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:25.384
-You are also in the new series
" A League of Their Own,"

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:26.986
which is fantastic.

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:28.320
-Thank you.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:33.192
-And you look a very
believable athlete in the show.

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:35.962
Were you a baseball player
in your youth?

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:37.863
-No.
-Okay.

00:06:37.863 --> 00:06:40.399
But, I mean, you obviously --
I mean, somebody --

00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:42.768
There had to be some sort of
coaching involved.

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:44.336
-Thank you.
There was coaching involved.

00:06:44.336 --> 00:06:46.171
-Okay.
-And that's all I'll say.

00:06:46.171 --> 00:06:50.409
No, I learned -- I knew nothing,
but now I think I sort of can --

00:06:50.409 --> 00:06:51.977
I kind of like
my swing, actually.

00:06:51.977 --> 00:06:53.812
I think I have --
You know, I was told --

00:06:53.812 --> 00:06:55.882
People wonder -- they said,
"You've played before,"

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:57.950
and I said "no,"
and they fell to their knees.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.485
They were shocked. Yeah.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:00.853
-That must be
a nice thing to get,

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:03.088
especially from people,
you know, who are obviously --

00:07:03.088 --> 00:07:04.290
their profession is coaching.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:05.791
-Yes, yes.
-Yeah.

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:08.127
And they just looked at you --
-I coach the coaches now, Seth.

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:09.261
It's crazy.

00:07:09.261 --> 00:07:10.830
-That's your new job
is to coach the coaches?

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.064
-Yeah.

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:14.400
-This is a very exciting time
to have you --

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.235
stand-up special,
"League of Their Own,"

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:18.204
and your off-Broadway show.

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:20.305
I'm so grateful
that you made time for us

00:07:20.305 --> 00:07:21.874
tonight and joined us.

00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:23.275
-I don't want to leave.
Are we done?

00:07:23.275 --> 00:07:24.977
I mean, this is -- Please, no.

00:07:24.977 --> 00:07:27.580
-Our time is up,
but you could stay if you want.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.514
-I'm going to stay.
They want me to stay.

00:07:29.514 --> 00:07:31.683
[ Cheers and applause ]
They want me to stay.

00:07:31.683 --> 00:07:33.252
-Kate Berlant, everybody.

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:34.787
"Kate Berlant:
Cinnamon in the Wind"

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:38.424
is now streaming on Hulu,
and her show "Kate"

00:07:38.424 --> 00:07:40.426
runs through October 8th at
the Connelly Theater.

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:41.894
We'll be right back with more
"Late Night."

